<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leutkirch im Allgäu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leutkirch im <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allgau">Allgäu</a> is a town in the Allgäu region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> that grew up as the market centre of the Nibelgau district. It was a free imperial city from the 1290s until 1802, a small council-governed town living from linen weaving, and passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and then, in 1810, to Württemberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leutkirch-im-allgau.jpg" alt="Leutkirch im Allgäu" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flodur63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leutkirch_-_Schloss_Zeil_-_Leutkirch_v_N_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
